# Commit gate — write the product changelog first

Admin **Instituto → Novedades del sistema** is fed by `src/lib/product-changelog/catalog.ts`. Staff only see what we write there.

## Before `git commit`

1. Ask: will a parent, student, teacher, or admin **notice** this after deploy?
2. If **yes**, add a new object at the **top** of `PRODUCT_CHANGELOG_ENTRIES` **before** creating the commit. Include that file in the **same** commit.
3. If **no**, skip the entry (see below). Do not invent filler.

Do **not** run `git commit` for product-visible work while the catalog still lacks this change.

## Entry shape

- `id`: kebab-case, unique, stable (`trial-classes`, not `update-2`).
- `date`: commit day `YYYY-MM-DD`.
- `area`: one of `PRODUCT_CHANGELOG_AREAS`.
- `title` / `summary`: `t(es, en, pt)` — staff-facing, one sentence each, no commit hashes or file lists.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — prepended, three locales, what staff can now do
{
  id: "section-share-photo",
  date: "2026-08-29",
  area: "academic",
  title: t("Foto para compartir la sección", "Section share photo", "Foto para partilhar a turma"),
  summary: t(
    "Cada sección puede tener una foto para el link de inscripción.",
    "Each section can have a photo on its enrollment link.",
    "Cada turma pode ter uma foto no link de inscrição.",
  ),
}

// ❌ BAD — committing a feature with no catalog row
git commit -m "feat: section share photo"
```

## Skip (no entry)

Docs/specs/plans, Cursor rules, tests-only, lint/deps/chore, refactors with **no** staff/family/student-visible change.

## Still do

Commit finished work per **`37-commit-finished-work-ask-when-mixed.mdc`**. This rule only adds the changelog step; it does not delay the commit.